1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,800
[Custom Paper Animation Intro — Ketan Chokkara | AI Engineer & Data Scientist]

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:11,500
Hi everyone! I'm Ketan Chokkara, an AI Engineer and Data Scientist from India.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:18,500
Today, I'm excited to present RelayDesk — an evidence-gated customer support triage and engineering escalation system...

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:23,000
...built for the Flip the Switch Hackathon on Switch AI.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,500
Every tech company faces a painful trade-off: either support teams over-escalate routine issues...

6
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,000
...and drown engineers in duplicate tickets, or ungrounded AI chatbots hallucinate false answers.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
RelayDesk solves this by coordinating human leads and autonomous Switch agents in a shared room...

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000
...where every single triage decision is strictly evidence-gated, and zero customer-facing action is taken without human approval.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,500
Let's look at Scenario 1: A customer reports a checkout 500 error after this morning's release.

10
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:57,000
Watch how our frontline agent, @relaydesk-triager, handles this in real time.

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,500
It normalizes the unstructured text, extracting the component, version, and exact error signature.

12
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:08,000
It queries our deterministic index and renders this formatted Evidence Card.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Notice the multi-feature score: 0.86 confidence, driven by symptom and version alignment against open incident INC-1042.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,500
Because 0.86 exceeds our duplicate threshold of 0.75, it issues a DECISION DUPLICATE card.

15
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:28,000
Notice the critical safety gate: It halts with 'Awaiting human operator approval'. No customer reply is sent until the lead signs off.

16
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Now let's see what happens with a brand-new, novel defect in Scenario 2.

17
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:40,500
Here, a customer reports a discount calculation failure in price_calculator on 10% discount orders.

18
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:46,000
@relaydesk-triager evaluates it against the knowledge base. The top candidate score is only 0.70...

19
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:52,500
...below our duplicate threshold. Recognizing this novel code defect, it selects DECISION ESCALATE...

20
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:57,500
...and tags our second agent, @relaydesk-investigator.

21
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:04,000
This is where Switch's multi-agent power shines: @relaydesk-investigator wakes up via agent-to-agent delegation.

22
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:11,500
Rather than guessing the cause, it copies the service into an isolated, disposable temporary sandbox and runs our pytest suite.

23
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:16,000
Look at the output card: REPRODUCTION RESULT — Bug Confirmed!

24
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,500
It captures the exact assertion failure — 134.98 versus expected 134.97...

25
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:29,000
...and identifies the exact root cause: the discount quantizer was using ROUND_DOWN instead of ROUND_HALF_UP!

26
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:35,500
It packages a ready-to-fix engineering ticket with full reproduction proof, awaiting operator sign-off.

27
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:40,500
RelayDesk completes the full workflow with two more tracks:

28
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:48,000
In Scenario 3, for stale search results, it grounds a verified answer from Runbook RB-501, drafting resolution steps.

29
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:56,000
In Scenario 4, when given a vague report with zero technical context, it refuses to hallucinate, issuing a DECISION CLARIFY card with a targeted diagnostic question.

30
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Finally, let's look at the engineering rigor in the terminal:

31
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:07,500
Running pytest — all 27 unit, integration, and hardened sandbox tests pass in just 0.2 seconds.

32
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:15,000
And on our strict held-out benchmark split, RelayDesk delivers 100% decision accuracy, 100% escalation precision, and 100% recall...

33
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:20,000
...with zero unsupported assertions and a median latency of under 0.5 milliseconds!

34
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:26,000
RelayDesk brings deterministic safety and human oversight to multi-agent support workflows with Switch.

35
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,000
The code is open source on GitHub. Thank you to WeMakeDevs and Switch AI!
